{
  "verdict": "sampling",
  "cause": "TEMPERATURE_HIGH",
  "fix": {"action": "set_param", "target": "temperature", "value": "0.7"},
  "rationale": "The user reports the breakage began right after they 'tuned the sampling to explore', and the request shows temperature 3.5, which flattens the token distribution enough to routinely sample low-probability tokens. The response shows exactly that: the code derails mid-function, the comments contradict themselves, and generation stops at 141 tokens (well under max_tokens 350) because an EOS token was sampled early. The repeat_penalty of 1.4 adds distortion, but temperature 3.5 alone is sufficient to produce non-running output, so it is the single root cause; lowering it to ~0.7 (and ideally also relaxing repeat_penalty toward 1.0-1.1) restores coherent code."
}

